{"kind":"example","label":"ex:per-nucleon-channel-decomposition","title":"Per-nucleon channel data for proton and neutron","html":"<a id=\"ex:per-nucleon-channel-decomposition\"></a><p>For each channel <code class=\"language-math math-inline\">c</code>, the per-nucleon Garside factor <code class=\"language-math math-inline\">G(c)</code> is the Frobenius matrix element of <code class=\"language-math math-inline\">\\Delta_3</code> in the <code class=\"language-math math-inline\">T_{2,3}</code> eigenvector <code class=\"language-math math-inline\">v_c</code>.</p>\n<p><strong>Proton</strong> (<code class=\"language-math math-inline\">\\mathfrak{p} = \\mathfrak{u}\\mathfrak{u}\\mathfrak{d}</code>), crossings:</p>\n<pre><code class=\"language-math math-display\">  \\sigma_0(\\mathfrak{u}\\mathfrak{u}) \\times [\\sigma_1 - \\tfrac{1}{2}h](\\mathfrak{u}\\mathfrak{d}) \\times [\\sigma_0 - \\tfrac{1}{2}h](\\mathfrak{u}\\mathfrak{d})</code></pre>\n<table>\n<thead>\n<tr>\n<th align=\"center\">Channel</th>\n<th align=\"center\"><code class=\"language-math math-inline\">\\lambda_c</code></th>\n<th align=\"center\"><code class=\"language-math math-inline\">G_P(c)</code></th>\n<th align=\"center\">Numeric at <code class=\"language-math math-inline\">q_0</code></th>\n</tr>\n</thead>\n<tbody>\n<tr>\n<td align=\"center\">Sym (Trivial)</td>\n<td align=\"center\"><code class=\"language-math math-inline\">q^3</code></td>\n<td align=\"center\"><code class=\"language-math math-inline\">q \\cdot \\tfrac{1}{2}[2]_q \\cdot \\tfrac{1}{2}[2]_q</code></td>\n<td align=\"center\"><code class=\"language-math math-inline\">+1.122</code></td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td align=\"center\">Std <code class=\"language-math math-inline\">\\lambda_1</code> (Unconf.)</td>\n<td align=\"center\"><code class=\"language-math math-inline\">-q</code></td>\n<td align=\"center\"><code class=\"language-math math-inline\">\\langle v_1, \\Delta_3 v_1 \\rangle_F</code></td>\n<td align=\"center\"><code class=\"language-math math-inline\">-1.174</code></td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td align=\"center\">Std <code class=\"language-math math-inline\">\\lambda_2</code> (Conf.)</td>\n<td align=\"center\"><code class=\"language-math math-inline\">q^{-1}</code></td>\n<td align=\"center\"><code class=\"language-math math-inline\">\\langle v_2, \\Delta_3 v_2 \\rangle_F</code></td>\n<td align=\"center\"><code class=\"language-math math-inline\">+0.858</code></td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td align=\"center\">Alt (Sign)</td>\n<td align=\"center\"><code class=\"language-math math-inline\">-q^{-3}</code></td>\n<td align=\"center\"><code class=\"language-math math-inline\">(-q^{-1}) \\cdot (-\\tfrac{1}{2}[2]_q)^2</code></td>\n<td align=\"center\"><code class=\"language-math math-inline\">-0.911</code></td>\n</tr>\n</tbody>\n</table>\n<p><strong>Channel sum:</strong> <code class=\"language-math math-inline\">a = \\sum_c G_P(c) = -h/2</code>.</p>\n<p><strong>Neutron</strong> (<code class=\"language-math math-inline\">\\mathfrak{n} = \\mathfrak{u}\\mathfrak{d}\\mathfrak{d}</code>), crossings:</p>\n<pre><code class=\"language-math math-display\">  [\\sigma_0 - \\tfrac{1}{2}h](\\mathfrak{u}\\mathfrak{d}) \\times [\\sigma_1 - h](\\mathfrak{d}\\mathfrak{d}) \\times [\\sigma_0 - \\tfrac{1}{2}h](\\mathfrak{u}\\mathfrak{d})</code></pre>\n<table>\n<thead>\n<tr>\n<th align=\"center\">Channel</th>\n<th align=\"center\"><code class=\"language-math math-inline\">\\lambda_c</code></th>\n<th align=\"center\"><code class=\"language-math math-inline\">G_N(c)</code></th>\n<th align=\"center\">Numeric at <code class=\"language-math math-inline\">q_0</code></th>\n</tr>\n</thead>\n<tbody>\n<tr>\n<td align=\"center\">Sym (Trivial)</td>\n<td align=\"center\"><code class=\"language-math math-inline\">q^3</code></td>\n<td align=\"center\"><code class=\"language-math math-inline\">\\tfrac{1}{2}[2]_q \\cdot q^{-1} \\cdot \\tfrac{1}{2}[2]_q</code></td>\n<td align=\"center\"><code class=\"language-math math-inline\">+0.9108</code></td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td align=\"center\">Std <code class=\"language-math math-inline\">\\lambda_1</code> (Unconf.)</td>\n<td align=\"center\"><code class=\"language-math math-inline\">-q</code></td>\n<td align=\"center\"><code class=\"language-math math-inline\">\\langle v_1, \\Delta_3 v_1 \\rangle_F</code></td>\n<td align=\"center\"><code class=\"language-math math-inline\">-1.2222</code></td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td align=\"center\">Std <code class=\"language-math math-inline\">\\lambda_2</code> (Conf.)</td>\n<td align=\"center\"><code class=\"language-math math-inline\">q^{-1}</code></td>\n<td align=\"center\"><code class=\"language-math math-inline\">\\langle v_2, \\Delta_3 v_2 \\rangle_F</code></td>\n<td align=\"center\"><code class=\"language-math math-inline\">+0.7995</code></td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td align=\"center\">Alt (Sign)</td>\n<td align=\"center\"><code class=\"language-math math-inline\">-q^{-3}</code></td>\n<td align=\"center\"><code class=\"language-math math-inline\">(-\\tfrac{1}{2}[2]_q) \\cdot (-q) \\cdot (-\\tfrac{1}{2}[2]_q)</code></td>\n<td align=\"center\"><code class=\"language-math math-inline\">-1.1221</code></td>\n</tr>\n</tbody>\n</table>\n<p><strong>Channel sum:</strong> <code class=\"language-math math-inline\">b = \\sum_c G_N(c) = -3(q^2-1)(q^2+1)^2/(4q^3)</code>.</p>\n<p>The values <code class=\"language-math math-inline\">\\{G_P(c), G_N(c)\\}</code> are algebraic functions of <code class=\"language-math math-inline\">q</code> and determine all nuclear Q-values via the branching factorization.</p>\n","source":"folio/quantum-observable-universe/nuclear-interactions/per-nucleon-channel-decomposition-example.md","heading":"Example","number":"14.10.2","page":"b/ex-per-nucleon-channel-decomposition"}
